<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>hyponoia</id>
    <version>0.3.1</version>
    <!-- packageSourceUrl points at the packaging, not the product: it is the
         first thing a Chocolatey moderator looks for, because it is how the
         next maintainer finds the nuspec that produced the package. -->
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia/tree/main/pkg/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>patalbansishashank</owners>
    <title>Hyponoia</title>
    <authors>patalbansishashank</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>mcp ai claude code-intelligence codebase developer-tools tree-sitter llm</tags>
    <summary>Fast code intelligence engine for AI coding agents</summary>
    <description>
hyponoia is a native MCP server distributed with authenticated
release-owned runtime assets. Chocolatey retains the complete extracted runtime
set and exposes its executable through a PATH shim.

Full indexes an average repository in milliseconds, the Linux kernel (28M LOC) in
3 minutes. Answers structural queries in under 1ms. Supports 158 languages via
vendored tree-sitter grammars. No hosted service or API key. Plug and play across
43 agent surfaces including Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, and Zed.

After installation, run:

    hyponoia install

to configure your coding agents automatically.
    </description>
    <!-- The tag this package actually installs. v0.8.1 stood here and 404s:
         it is a DeusData-era version from the inherited tag line, and it
         survived every version bump because nothing follows this URL. It is
         the one field in the nuspec that is not derived from $version. -->
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/patalbansishashank/hyponoia/releases/tag/v0.3.1</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
